cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use Indicium, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "Indicium: a standard for typed scientific claims bound to their evidence"
version: 2.0.0
authors:
  - family-names: Nothias
    given-names: Louis-Félix
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0001-6711-6719"
    affiliation: "Holobiomics Lab, CNRS / Université Côte d'Azur"
repository-code: "https://github.com/HolobiomicsLab/indicium"
license: MIT
abstract: >-
  Indicium is a versioned standard for a typed scientific claim bound to the
  evidence that grounds it. One LinkML schema generates pydantic models, JSON
  Schema, SHACL shapes and an OWL ontology. The claim structure follows the
  Bucur et al. SuperPattern; evidence, citation, document and provenance types
  reuse ECO, CiTO, DoCO, IAO, FaBiO, SEPIO and PROV-O. What Indicium defines is
  the binding: a claim, its typed evidence, and the source that evidence points
  to.
keywords:
  - scientific claims
  - evidence
  - provenance
  - LinkML
  - SHACL
  - ECO
  - CiTO
  - SEPIO
  - PROV-O
